  "summary": "Lyon Cathedral was begun in 1175 on a Romanesque plan that was converted to Gothic during building, and it shows the transition in its choir and transept. It sits on a cramped site between hill and river, which kept the nave short. It is known for its 14th-century astronomical clock and stained glass, and for hosting two ecumenical councils.",
